## Troubleshooting

| Problem | Why it happens | Fix |
|---------|---------------|-----|
| `Too many command line arguments` on terraform plan | PowerShell splits on `=` in unquoted flags | Use `terraform plan -out="aum-lab.tfplan"` (quoted) |
| `Backend initialization required` | Backend config changed or new session | Run `terraform init -reconfigure` |
| Wrong content in module folder | File written to wrong path during setup | Run `Select-String 'variable' modules\keyvault\main.tf \| Select-Object -First 1` — if it shows `subnet_id` the compute content is in the wrong folder. Overwrite with correct content. |
| `403 Forbidden` on Key Vault secret | `enable_rbac_authorization` missing | Confirm `enable_rbac_authorization = true` is in `modules/keyvault/main.tf`. Re-run apply. |
| `SkuNotAvailable: Standard_B2s` | Capacity restrictions in eastus | Use `Standard_D2s_v3` — already set in this lab's compute module |
| `400 ResourceIdentityRequired` on policy | Modify-effect policies require a managed identity | The update-manager module includes `identity { type = "SystemAssigned" }` — if you see this your module has outdated content |
| `400 Patch orchestration mode is not set` | VMs missing `patch_mode = AutomaticByPlatform` | The compute module sets this on all three VMs — if you see this your module has outdated content |
| `start_date_time` error during plan | Date in `update-manager/main.tf` is in the past | Update to any future date: `"YYYY-MM-DD HH:MM"` |
| Assessment returns `ResourceGroupNotFound` | `$subId` variable was empty | Run `$subId = az account show --query id -o tsv` then `echo $subId` to confirm it printed a GUID |
| `ConvertFrom-Json: Unexpected character 'A'` | `az vm assess-patches` outputting a table, not JSON | Ensure `-o json` flag is in the script — the `validate-lab.ps1` in this repo already includes it |
| DC01 extension fails or times out | AD promotion failure or Azure timeout | Re-run `terraform apply` — Terraform retries only what failed |
| WS01/WS02 domain join fails | DC01 took longer than expected to promote | Re-run `terraform apply` — the join script waits for DNS resolution before attempting `Add-Computer` |

